        <!-- art start -->
        <div class="art">
           <h2 class="art-tit">Stapokibart Injection Approved for Marketing by China NMPA</h2>
          <div class="art-info">
            <p>
<span>CCFDIE</span><i>|</i>
<span>Updated: 2025-02-19</span>
</p>
            <div class="art-share">
              <a onClick="javascript:;" data-share="facebook" class="icon-share icon-share1">&nbsp;</a>
            <a onClick="javascript:;" data-share="twitter" class="icon-share icon-share2">&nbsp;</a>
            <a onClick="javascript:;" data-share="linkedin" class="icon-share icon-share3">&nbsp;</a>
            </div>
             </div>
          <!--enpproperty <articleid>1073588</articleid><date>2025-02-19 19:53:27.0</date><author></author><title>Stapokibart Injection Approved for Marketing by China NMPA</title><keyword></keyword><subtitle></subtitle><introtitle></introtitle><siteid>48</siteid><nodeid>16569</nodeid><nodename>Regulatory Information</nodename><nodesearchname>2@NMPA</nodesearchname>/enpproperty--><div class="art-text">       
          <p><!--enpcontent--><p>Recently, the Stapokibart Injection (trade name: 康悦达) of Chengdu Kangnuoxing Biopharma, Inc. is approved by China NMPA. It is indicated for the treatment of adult patients with moderate-to-severe atopic dermatitis in adults who are inadequately controlled by topical medications or for whom topical medications are not indicated.</p><p>The Stapokibart Injection is a monoclonal antibody drug targeting IL-4Rα, which treats atopic dermatitis induced by excessive inflammatory response by blocking the binding of IL-4 and IL-13 to IL-4Rα receptor and inhibiting the release of downstream inflammatory factors, protein expression and inflammatory cell activity caused by IL-4 and IL-13.</p><p>The marketing of this product provides a new treatment option for adult patients with moderate-to-severe atopic dermatitis.</p><!--/enpcontent--></p>
        </div>
        </div>
        <!-- art end -->
      
